    "screens_the_bare_core_test_passed_but_the_full_stack_does_not": [
      "ELP43_I43"
    ],
    "finding": "ELP38 is 12.35 mm bare (core + I plate, worst case); the known stack adds 0.14 mm of glue, label, clamp and pocket, leaving 3.51 mm of the 16 mm D1 budget for TIM, cold plate and fastener heads -- 1.51 mm beyond the 2 mm policy reserve. ELP43_I43 passed the bare-core reserve test but fails it once glue and label are counted. ELP32 is the only set that fits D3's 10 mm flat (by 0.06 mm) and it loses that margin the moment a clamp is added. Height is not the only screen: of the sets that clear the reserve, only ELP38_I38 also passes the three-turn area screen at the RFQ fault current, so the D1 core choice is still a trade between a core that fits and a core that does not saturate -- not a settled answer.",
